      <body>
         <entry xml:id="domini-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">דומיני</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">dwmyny</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">domini</pron>
               <gramGrp opt="false">
                  <gram type="pos" opt="false">noun</gram>
                  <gram type="gen" opt="false">m.</gram>
                  <gram type="mod">vocative</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="domini-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>Lord</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="la">
                  <quote>dominus</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>למה הדבר דומה למלך ואפרכוס שהיו נתונין בקרוכין והיו בני המדינה מבקשים לומר למלך 
                     <app>
                        <lem>דומיני</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#V">דומינו</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#K Ox1 Ox2">הינמון</rdg>
                     </app> ולא היו יודעין אי זהו, מה עשה המלך דחפו והשליכו 
                     <app>
                        <lem>מן</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#K Ox1 Ox2 V">חוץ</rdg>
                     </app> הקרוכין 
                     <app>
                        <lem>וידעו את המלך</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#K V">וידעו הכל שהוא איפרכוס</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat2 Ox1 Ox2">וידעו הכל שהוא אפרכוס</rdg>
                     </app></quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">8,10</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">I 64: 1</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">קרוכין</ref>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">אפרכוס</ref>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">הינמון</ref>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">איפרכוס</ref>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>To what may this be compared? To a king and a prefect who sat in a chariot, and the residents of the province wished to say “Domine!” to the king, but they didn’t know who [of the two] is the king. What did the king do? He pushed the prefect and thrust him out of the chariot, so that they knew who was the king.</quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">KohR 6,1</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">דומינין</term>); <bibl type="ancient">MidrZ Koh 6,10</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">הימנון</term>); <bibl type="ancient">Yalq 147 [8a: 22]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">המנון</term>); <bibl type="ancient">Yalq Jes 394 [387d: 57]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">המנון</term>) ; <bibl type="ancient">YalqM Jes 2,22 [25: 23]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">הינמון</term>)</note>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>Cf. <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">הנמנון</ref></note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Krauss, LW II</title>
                  <citedRange>190b-191a</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
